========================================================================================
  PASS: the Ewald kernel is supercell-invariant to machine precision.
  Every M describes the same physical layer and now returns the same
  number, which is an IDENTITY rather than a tolerance being met.

  Read the two rows together, because they say different things. The
  image ladder stalls at a spread of 1.36e-01 after 16 shells -- it
  converges only as 1/n_img, so it shrinks the truncation without
  removing it. Ewald removes it outright, in one shot, at cutoff 4.

  THE TRUE FLOOR IS 1.4290e-03. At M = 4, the value used
  throughout the convergence campaign, the old kernel gave 3.8852e-03,
  so 63% of what was reported as the discretisation floor
  was this artifact. Every quantitative result from that campaign needs
  RE-RUNNING, not merely reinterpreting.

  Note the 1/M fit's extrapolation to M -> infinity was 1.1185e-3; the
  exact answer is 1.4290e-03. The fit described the truncation well
  but its intercept was not the floor -- another reason to re-run rather
  than to correct old numbers arithmetically.
========================================================================================
